            <title>[LU-21257] sanity test_300d: mds1: import is not in FULL state after 50, test_300e then fails: set striped dir error</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21257</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;This issue was created by maloo for Patrickbot &amp;lt;patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This issue relates to the following test suite run: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/9b2b913c-e7ee-4ebb-86d0-85f701a1e314" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/9b2b913c-e7ee-4ebb-86d0-85f701a1e314&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test session details:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Client&lt;br/&gt;
Lustre: 2.17.61.86&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Build: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/136090" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/136090&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Kernel: 4.18.0-553.177.1.el8_10.x86_64&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Server&lt;br/&gt;
Lustre: 2.17.61.86&lt;br/&gt;
Branch: master&lt;br/&gt;
Build: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/136090" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/136090&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
Kernel: 4.18.0-553.177.1.el8_10_lustre.x86_64&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;sanity test_300d fails in its precheck, before touching anything:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;  wait_osc_import_state mds ost$i FULL&lt;br/&gt;
  sanity test_300d: FAIL: mds1: import is not in FULL state after 50&lt;br/&gt;
  (or "mds2: ...", an OSC import of an MDT stuck in CONNECTING)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;sanity test_300e then fails right after with&lt;br/&gt;
  mkdir: cannot create directory '/mnt/lustre/d300e.sanity': Input/output error&lt;br/&gt;
  sanity test_300e: FAIL: set striped dir error&lt;br/&gt;
because the client has lost its connection to an MDT (evicted).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Seen on review sessions of unrelated changes since 2026-11-04, none on the branch itself:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class="alternate" type="square"&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;70792 ps1 review-ldiskfs-dne (this test set), session 313d53cb-421d-4103-bda5-46344c379e0a&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;70254 ps2 review-ldiskfs-dne, session f8e71349-6a71-4258-87c6-a63450c22a4c&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;63189 ps7 review-dne-selinux-ssk-part-1, session 96aacfa8-afcb-41dc-8674-5aebd09b7dee&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;69035 ps10 review-dne-ipv6, session 260711f5-c786-4037-9f53-455950ecee0d&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;71146 ps1 review-dne-ipv6, session 7aef9116-7ee0-4ad6-85dc-7ed4077c1182&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Rate is about 0.1% of sanity runs per group (rainshadow test sanity 300d). The 71146 patch only changes quota code, which 300d/300e do not touch. In 71146's session the node of MDT0001 also logged "ICMPv6: NA: &amp;lt;mac&amp;gt; advertised our address &amp;lt;its address&amp;gt;" 78 times (a duplicate IPv6 address on the test network), so that one may be infrastructure, but the other sessions are IPv4 trevis clusters with the same sequence. &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20789" title="sanity test_300d: @@@@@@ FAIL: wrong stripe 1 for /mnt/lustre/d300d.sanity/striped_dir/f1 " class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20789"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20789&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; (300d "wrong stripe 1", fixed by change 69059) is a different error and is in all these builds.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-71146-ps1-b55335531322 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/71146" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/71146&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;



